SUPLINF.P:
In paragraph (c)(2) “Action by BIS,” this rule corrects and clarifies the NAC notification process. The AC/S IFR stated that BIS would notify you if you may use NAC. However, this rule clarifies that after the notification has been registered in SNAP-R and within twenty-five calendar days, BIS will inform you if a license is required. If BIS has not contacted you, then System for Tracking Export License Applications (STELA) (
https://snapr.bis.doc.gov/stela
) will, on the twenty-fifth calendar day following the date of registration, provide either confirmation that you can use License Exception NAC and a NAC confirmation number to be submitted in AES or confirmation that you cannot use License Exception NAC and you must apply for a license to continue with the transaction.

